  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 14 files needed to trace this exception path, most important first:\n\n**Netty (origin + propagation):**\n1. `transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/nio/AbstractNioByteChannel.java` \u2014 `NioByteUnsafe.handleReadException()` is where an `IOException` (e.g. \"Connection reset by peer\") on a socket read becomes `pipeline.fireExceptionCaught(cause)`, the actual origin point.\n2. `transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/DefaultChannelPipeline.java` \u2014 default pipeline implementation, including tail-context behavior when `exceptionCaught` isn't handled by user code.\n3. `transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/ChannelPipeline.java`, `ChannelHandlerContext.java`, `ChannelInboundHandler.java`, `ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 the exception-propagation contract (`fireExceptionCaught`) handlers rely on.\n\n**Spring (wrapping + translation):**\n4. `spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/http/server/reactive/ReactorHttpHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 the actual seam where reactor-netty's `HttpServerRequest`/`HttpServerResponse` get adapted into Spring's `HttpHandler` contract.\n5. `ReactorServerHttpRequest.java` / `ReactorServerHttpResponse.java` \u2014 wrap reactor-netty request/response, hold the reference to the underlying Netty `Channel`.\n6. `spring-web/src/main/java/org/springframework/web/server/adapter/HttpWebHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 **this is where error context is lost**: `handleUnresolvedError()` collapses any unhandled exception into a bare 500 (or silently drops it if it string-matches \"broken pipe\"/\"connection reset by peer\"/a fixed set of exception class names), discarding the original Netty exception type and stack.\n7. `WebHttpHandlerBuilder.java`, `ExceptionHandlingWebHandler.java`, `WebExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 the exception-handler chain assembled around the `WebHandler`, invoked before falling through to `HttpWebHandlerAdapter`'s catch-all.\n8. `spring-web/spring-web.gradle` \u2014 confirms `reactor-netty-http` is an **optional** dependency of spring-web, not vendored in this repo, so the middle hop (reactor-netty's own channel-to-`HttpServerRequest`/`HttpServerResponse` translation) is outside both indexed repositories and is the actual blind spot in the trace.",
